# Copy to .env and fill in:  cp .env.example .env
# .env is git-ignored.
#
# READ THIS FIRST: there is very little here on purpose.
#
# Until 2026-08-24 this file described the superseded architecture — Redis
# hosts, a Grafana admin password, a Kubernetes master node IP, container
# image tags. None of those components exist any more (ADR-002). Anyone who
# filled this in was configuring a system that had already been deleted.
#
# The hybrid backend reads exactly three settings, all of them from
# services/backend/core/config.py::Settings via pydantic-settings, which
# matches these names case-insensitively. None of the three is a secret.

# ── Backend (Lambda) ─────────────────────────────────────────
# After `terraform apply`, Terraform sets these three as environment variables
# on both Lambda functions from its own outputs — you do NOT fill them in for
# a deployed environment. This file is for running backend code outside
# Lambda, which today means ad-hoc scripts only; there is no supported local
# application run (see README "Running the tests").
#
# Leaving either of the first two empty makes authentication fail CLOSED:
# the app starts, answers /health, and authenticates nobody. /ready reports
# that as not_ready rather than letting it look healthy.
#   terraform output cognito_user_pool_id
COGNITO_USER_POOL_ID=
#   terraform output cognito_app_client_id
COGNITO_APP_CLIENT_ID=
COGNITO_REGION=ap-southeast-1

# ── Local tooling only ───────────────────────────────────────
# Read by scripts/backup-tables.sh; defaults to ap-southeast-1 if unset.
AWS_REGION=ap-southeast-1
# Which local AWS credential profile the CLI scripts should use.
AWS_PROFILE=

# ── Not here, deliberately ───────────────────────────────────
# Terraform variables live in terraform/terraform.tfvars (see
# terraform/terraform.tfvars.example) — not in this file.
# CI has no static AWS keys at all: the deploy workflow authenticates through
# GitHub OIDC against the role in terraform/modules/github-oidc.
# The agent stores its own API key in ~/.aiops-agent/config.json, written by
# `aiops-agent register`, never in an env var.
